Problem: Subarray Sum Equals K (LC 560)

Pattern: Prefix Sum + Hash Map

Approach
Store mp[0] = 1 to represent a prefix sum of 0 before the array starts.
Traverse the array while maintaining prefixSum.

Calculate:

need = prefixSum - k;

If need exists in the map:

count += mp[need];

Store the current prefix sum:

mp[prefixSum]++;
Return count.
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(n)